# UI design source (Figma)

Figma file **Nagara** is the design source of truth for the `public/`
redesign — for how things **look** (colors, type, layout, composition),
not for what things **are**. Information architecture, the field
inventory, widget behavior, and data shapes are owned by the schema
(`src/models/character.mts`), the ADRs, and `docs/` — when a frame lags
or contradicts those, the schema wins on content and Figma wins on look.
The live client may still lag — see **ui-navigation-playbook**. Adapt MCP
output to this stack (vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, ADR-012, **styling** /
**hypertext**).

- File: https://www.figma.com/design/n61wtRUXEaxhSc2gnL640J/Nagara
- `fileKey`: `n61wtRUXEaxhSc2gnL640J`
- Pages, after a divider: one per app view — `Welcome`, `Dashboard`,
  `Creation`, `Character`, `Picker` (ids in the table below). Each holds
  the view's canonical frame (approved designs only) and, once the view
  has design rounds, a `<view> — explorations` section beside it (drafts,
  rejected options, state demos)
- Page: `Components` (`944:15`) — the reusable component library, one
  section per layer: `Foundations` (`1403:14`, sheet `1403:15`, a token /
  type sheet), `Icons` (`1403:224`, sheet `1416:2`), `Atoms` (`1403:225`,
  sheet `1440:9`), `Molecules` (`1403:226`, sheet `1481:111`),
  `Organisms` (`1403:227`, sheet `1573:977`), plus `Explorations`
  (`1601:3358`, boards comparing options for the library itself, e.g.
  palette candidates). Variables: `Primitives`
  (colours hidden from pickers) and `Semantic` (aliases components bind
  to); every variable carries its CSS name as WEB code syntax.
- **Design rules** — how the library is named, extended and drafted in
  rounds, tokens, palette roles, motion, focus, responsive layouts and
  the hand-drawn asset briefs — live in
  [`docs/design-system.md`](../../docs/design-system.md) (`DS §anchor`
  cites). This rule only maps the file.
- The MCP cannot load the TorukSC font (Display; it is installed only on
  the user's machine) — clone an existing TorukSC text node instead of
  creating one.

Parse share URLs as `fileKey` + `node-id` (hyphens → colons for MCP
`nodeId`). Ignore `t=` query params. Local Variables only — no published
library; Code Connect needs an Organization plan.

Figma skills (`figma-design-to-code`, `figma-use`, …) are served by the
Figma MCP server; if one is not installed locally, read
`skill://figma/<name>/SKILL.md` via `get_figma_skill`.

**Call budget.** The account holds a Professional plan with a Full seat
(since 2026-10-26, kept for the design work and likely dropped after it):
Figma allows 200 MCP calls per day and 10 per minute (Figma's MCP
rate-limits doc). Within that there is no per-call rationing: screenshot
your own builds and drafts to check them, and read frames, metadata and
variables whenever the task benefits. The write-only-on-request rule below
still applies. **If a call fails with a plan or rate-limit error,** the seat
has probably lapsed to Starter (about 20 calls a month for every MCP tool,
`use_figma` included). Stop, tell the user, and switch to frugal mode: no
screenshots of your own work, one `get_design_context` per frame, and reuse
results instead of re-fetching.

